lse},"event":"closed","commit_id":"1ad7e7c0be2c85e4c8f6770477b26575d6b4dc27","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/commits/1ad7e7c0be2c85e4c8f6770477b26575d6b4dc27","created_at":"2016-06-07T22:26:21Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/236099627","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/2618#issuecomment-236099627","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/2618","id":236099627,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjA5OTYyNw==","user":{"login":"ndp","id":54177,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54177?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp","html_url":"https://github.com/ndp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-29T05:45:54Z","updated_at":"2016-07-29T05:46:26Z","body":"I apologize for commenting on a closed bug. I've been unable to get rxjs-es to work well, and this seemed like the same hoisting problem still. As stated in the bug above, ES6 code:\n\n```\n  // assign.js of RxJS\n  import { root } from './root';\n  const Object = root.Object;\n```\n\nconverts to `var Object = _root.root.Object;`, which has the `Object` var that is hoisted and masks webpack code trying to build the exports. When I rewrite the function with `const obj = root.Object;`, the problem is avoided. \n\n It does seem like it may be cleanly stated:\n\n>    If within an imported es6 module you use the construct `const Object = [anything]` \n>    to define a local const/variable, the code generated by Webpack creates a local `var` \n>    named `Object` that interferes with the ability of webpack to bundle, breaking lines\n>    such as `Object.defineProperty(...)`.\n\nSo... using `Object` as your own variable seems like a risky prospect, but I don't see it's a reserved word (http://www.ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-reserved-words), so I am assuming this is legit and should be supported.\n\nI've tried a few combinations Webpack 2.1.0-beta-8, 11, 12, 20 with similar versions as listed above and rxjs-es v5.0.0-beta.10. \n\nHere's one set of deps that fails:\n    \"babel-loader\": \"^6.2.4\",\n    \"babel-preset-es2015\": \"^6.6.0\",\n    \"babel-preset-es2015-webpack\": \"^6.4.0\",\n    \"copy-webpack-plugin\": \"^0.2.0\",\n    \"webpack\": \"^2.1.0-beta.12\",\n    \"rxjs-es\": \"^5.0.0-beta.20\",\n    \"webpack-dev-server\": \"latest\"\n\nHere is  a repo where I was able to isolate it, if that will help:\nhttps://github.com/ndp/tests/tree/rxjs-es-babel-hmmm\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/236099627/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ndp","id":54177,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54177?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp","html_url":"https://github.com/ndp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ndp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/236120817","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/2618#issuecomment-236120817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/2618","id":236120817,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjEyMDgxNw==","user":{"login":"Jessidhia","id":73085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMDg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia","html_url":"https://github.com/Jessidhia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-29T08:11:07Z","updated_at":"2016-07-29T08:13:24Z","body":"This would still be a problem even without webpack converting the `const Object` to `var Object`. `Object` would just be in the temporal dead-zone when the import runs.\n\nThe only ways around it is to either internally rename the module-scope `Object` to, say, `_Object`; wrap the module code that runs after the `import`s are evaluated in an IIFE, or use `global.Object` in places where webpack tries to call into `Object`...\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/236120817/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Jessidhia","id":73085,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczMDg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73085?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia","html_url":"https://github.com/Jessidhia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jessidhia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/236121210","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/2618#issuecomment-236121210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/2618","id":236121210,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzNjEyMTIxMA==","user":{"login":"sokra","id":1365881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjU4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1365881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra","html_url":"https://github.com/sokra","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sokra/